API (streaming — recommended)API (non-streaming) <p>Returns a server-sent event (SSE) stream with partial tokens as they are generated:</p> <pre><code>POST /api/chat/stream
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "conversationId": "&lt;uuid&gt;",
  "message": "What decisions did we make about the database?"
}
</code></pre> <p>SSE events: <pre><code>data: {"type":"token","content":"We decided "}
data: {"type":"token","content":"to use PostgreSQL "}
data: {"type":"citations","citations":[{"objectId":"...","title":"Use PostgreSQL"}]}
data: {"type":"done"}
</code></pre></p> <pre><code>POST /api/chat/{conversationId}/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "user",
  "content": "What decisions did we make about the database?"
}
</code></pre>

Field Description <code>name</code> Display name for this integration <code>providerType</code> The provider: <code>google_drive</code>, <code>gmail</code>, <code>github</code>, <code>trale</code>, <code>web</code> <code>sourceType</code> Category of content: <code>drive</code>, <code>email</code>, <code>repo</code>, <code>meeting</code>, <code>web</code> <code>syncMode</code> <code>manual</code> (sync only when you trigger it) or <code>scheduled</code> (automatic on the interval). <code>recurring</code> is accepted as an alias for <code>scheduled</code>. A <code>manual</code> source never syncs on its own, and switching a source to <code>manual</code> clears its stored interval. <code>syncIntervalMinutes</code> Minutes between automatic syncs. Required in spirit for <code>scheduled</code>: omitting it applies the provider's default (60 minutes for the web crawler and Gmail). Ignored for <code>manual</code>. <code>enabled</code> Write-only on update: <code>false</code> pauses the source (<code>status: disabled</code>), <code>true</code> resumes it. Applied to a <code>needs_reconnect</code> source, <code>true</code> is an explicit retry — it returns the source to <code>active</code> and the next failure parks it again. <code>status</code> <code>active</code> (admitted for scheduled sync) · <code>needs_reconnect</code> (the stored credential was rejected — reconnect it; scheduled syncs stop) · <code>disabled</code> (paused; never admitted). See Reconnecting a source. <p>For <code>google_drive</code>, <code>config.folders</code> is the sync scope:</p> <pre><code>{
  "config": {
    "folders": [
      { "folder_id": "1AbC…", "name": "Reports", "drive_id": "" },
      { "folder_id": "1XyZ…", "name": "Shared contracts", "drive_id": "0AFt…" }
    ],
    "mime_types": ["application/pdf"],
    "recursive": true
  }
}
</code></pre> <p>When you write <code>folders</code> directly, <code>name</code> and <code>drive_id</code> are stored as you send them — send both so the UI and sync can label the target. Only <code>PUT /sync-targets</code> resolves them from Drive for you (see below). The legacy single-target keys <code>folder_id</code> and <code>shared_drive_id</code> are accepted and normalized into <code>folders</code>.</p>

CLIAPI <pre><code>memory documents delete &lt;doc-id&gt; --project my-project
</code></pre> <pre><code>DELETE /api/documents/{id}
</code></pre> <p>Bulk delete: <pre><code>DELETE /api/documents
{ "ids": ["doc_1", "doc_2"] }
</code></pre></p> <p>Warning</p> <p>Deleting a document removes its chunks and embeddings. Graph objects extracted from it are not automatically deleted — they remain in the graph.</p>
